/* i18n.js — INFINICUS multi-language engine (20 languages, one file)
 *
 * Install: upload i18n.js AND the i18n/ folder (one small file per language) to the
 * repo root, then add ONE line as the first thing inside <head> of index.html
 *     <script src="/i18n.js?v=1"></script>
 * Language files load on demand from /i18n/<code>.js (only the chosen language).
 * Bump ?v= whenever this file changes (sw.js serves non-HTML files cache-first).
 *
 * How it works: the page stays written in English. This file holds a table of
 * English UI phrases and their translations. It swaps the text of every
 * matching text node, placeholder, title and aria-label, and keeps watching the
 * page so text that JavaScript builds later (toasts, results) is translated too.
 * Anything without a translation stays in English, so nothing can break.
 *
 * Replaces the old applyLang()/TRANSLATIONS system (the old function is
 * overridden at DOMContentLoaded; the old table can be deleted later).
 * Right-to-left languages (ar, ur, fa) set <html dir="rtl">.
 *
 * API (window.InfinicusI18n): get() set(code) languages onChange(fn) t(englishText)
 * Storage key: inf_lang (same key the old system used).
 *
 * Limits: sentences assembled from variables (e.g. "Day ${n} of ${m}") and long
 * paragraphs (>110 chars) are not in the table and stay English; the PDF plan
 * window and the share-card image are generated separately and are not covered.
 * Translations are machine-drafted: have a native speaker review wording.
 */
